- The exact method of creating fragmentation may vary based on the underlying system implementation.
- Actual available memory (end result) may vary based on different `malloc` implementations and system specifics but this model should justify increased requirements for virtual space.

This example forces inefficiencies in memory allocation by ensuring each allocation request crosses a page boundary, thus resulting in inflated virtual memory usage while keeping actual dynamic memory usage low.

